{"id": "EUVD-2025-211004", "enisaUuid": "899efe89-934c-3fa0-95a7-3e6bcc7b347b", "description": "The SOAP HTTP client guards its response buffer growth with a check that relies on signed integer overflow, which is undefined behaviour and is not guaranteed to trigger. When the check is optimised away, a malicious SOAP server can make the client allocate a buffer far smaller than the data it then writes into it, producing a heap buffer overflow.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T20:26:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-25T20:44:13", "baseScore": 6.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:H", "references": ["https://github.com/php/php-src/security/advisories/GHSA-cj93-vc83-wgqv"], "aliases": ["CVE-2025-14181"], "assigner": "php", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05fbfeff-0c21-314c-b467-96f1307bcbc5", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.4.* <8.4.26"}, {"id": "47a8e683-0ff8-3bac-b84b-f07e7340c12f", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.3.* <8.3.35"}, {"id": "af8ca93e-fa58-3fd2-a85b-c81fcff7ae43", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.2.* <8.2.34"}, {"id": "f3bf28e7-b898-3f2c-b403-f6beaef9c657", "product": {"name": "PHP", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}, "product_version": "8.5.* <8.5.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5393ee42-63ed-318e-a329-9afe29fb6ecc", "vendor": {"name": "PHP Group"}}], "isExploited": false}